      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for saying that. it's such a relief to hear someone else see how this works. because nobody else at the office will say anything, and they're all just acting like it's normal, i've started feeling like i'm the one losing it. but the way the schedule shifts right when i'm most productive... it's too precise to be luck. \n\nsince they're being so careful to keep it \"subtle,\" do you think there are certain ways they might be using the company's official digital tools—like Slack or project management software—to keep tabs on my mental state or find ways to trigger me? i want to know what to watch out for so they don't think they've successfully gaslighted me.",
